{
  "id": "25254_mikubiru",
  "headword": "{見|み}くびる",
  "reading": "みくびる",
  "romaji": "mikubiru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan, transitive)",
  "gloss": "to underestimate; to look down on; to make light of",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to underestimate; to look down on; to make light of",
      "explanation": "to judge someone or something as less capable or important than they actually are"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25254_mikubiru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{相手|あいて}を{見|み}くびるな。",
      "english": "Don't underestimate your opponent.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25254_mikubiru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{実力|じつりょく}を{見|み}くびっていた。",
      "english": "I had underestimated his ability.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25254_mikubiru_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{問題|もんだい}を{見|み}くびると{大変|たいへん}なことになる。",
      "english": "If you underestimate this problem, it will turn into a serious matter.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25254_mikubiru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{私|わたし}を{見|み}くびらないでほしい。",
      "english": "I don't want you to look down on me.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A godan verb meaning to underestimate or belittle someone. Carries a stronger emotional charge than {甘|あま}く{見|み}る, implying contempt or dismissiveness toward the other person's capabilities.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {相手|あいて}を{見|み}くびる: to underestimate one's opponent\n- {実力|じつりょく}を{見|み}くびる: to underestimate someone's ability\n- {見|み}くびってはいけない: must not underestimate\n- {見|み}くびられる: to be looked down on\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {甘|あま}く{見|み}る: to take lightly or underestimate; less confrontational and more commonly used in everyday speech\n- {侮|あなど}る: to despise or hold in contempt; more literary and carries a stronger sense of scorn\n- {舐|な}める: (colloquial) to look down on or not take seriously; slangy and blunt\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nFrom {見|み} (looking) + くびる (an archaic verb meaning to count or reckon low), literally meaning to regard as being of low value.",
